{
  "info": {
    "name": "HustleHub+ API",
    "_postman_id": "7f3c1e20-4b9a-4d61-9f2e-8c5a1d0b3e77",
    "description": "# HustleHub+ API - Part 1\n\nCovers user registration, login and the existing marketplace endpoints.\n\n## Running the collection\n\n1. Start MongoDB, then run `npm run certs` once, then `npm start`.\n2. Check the `baseUrl` collection variable matches the port in your `.env` (default `https://localhost:5001`).\n3. The API uses a self-signed certificate, so turn off Settings > General > SSL certificate verification in Postman.\n4. Run the whole collection with the Postman runner, or send the requests individually from the top down.\n\nEvery run generates fresh email addresses, so the collection can be run repeatedly without clearing the database.\n\n## What is asserted\n\nAlongside each request its own tests, every response in the collection is checked to confirm it is JSON and that it never contains a password hash, a file path or a stack trace.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{authToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Runs after every request in the collection. These are the guarantees",
          "// that must hold no matter which endpoint was called or how it failed.",
          "pm.test('Response is JSON, not an HTML error page', function () {",
          "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('application/json');",
          "});",
          "",
          "pm.test('Response exposes no internal detail', function () {",
          "    var text = pm.response.text();",
          "    var markers = ['node_modules', 'INSY7314-POE', 'at JSON.parse', 'MongoServerError'];",
          "    markers.forEach(function (marker) {",
          "        pm.expect(text).to.not.include(marker);",
          "    });",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "https://localhost:5001",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Registration - successful",
      "description": "The happy paths required by the brief. Each run generates a fresh email address so the collection can be run repeatedly without clearing the database.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register a Client",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// A unique address per run keeps this request repeatable, and is reused",
                  "// later by the duplicate-email tests.",
                  "var address = 'client.' + Date.now() + '@example.com';",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('clientEmail', address);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('clientEmailUpper', address.toUpperCase());"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 201', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "var body = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Reports success', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.success).to.be.true;",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message).to.eql('Registration successful');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Returns the created account', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data).to.have.property('_id');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data.email).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('clientEmail').toLowerCase());",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Defaults the role to Client', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data.role).to.eql('Client');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Never returns the password', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data).to.not.have.property('password');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response body contains no password hash', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.not.include('$2b$');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Registers an account with no role supplied, which should default to Client.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Dylan Olsen\",\n  \"email\": \"{{clientEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"Str0ng!Pass\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Register a Freelancer",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('freelancerEmail', 'freelancer.' + Date.now() + '@example.com');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 201', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Stores the requested role', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.role).to.eql('Freelancer');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response body contains no password hash', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.not.include('$2b$');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Registers an account with an explicitly chosen, permitted role.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Bob Jones\",\n  \"email\": \"{{freelancerEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"An0ther!Pw\",\n  \"role\": \"Freelancer\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Unexpected fields are ignored",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('extraEmail', 'extra.' + Date.now() + '@example.com');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 201', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "var body = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Ignores the _id supplied by the caller', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data._id).to.not.eql('000000000000000000000000');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Does not store the unexpected fields', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data).to.not.have.property('isAdmin');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data.createdAt).to.not.include('1999');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Sends _id, createdAt and isAdmin alongside the real fields. The API should discard them rather than write them to the new document, which is the defence against mass assignment.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Mass Assignment\",\n  \"email\": \"{{extraEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"Str0ng!Pass\",\n  \"_id\": \"000000000000000000000000\",\n  \"isAdmin\": true,\n  \"createdAt\": \"1999-01-01T00:00:00.000Z\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "auth": {
        "type": "noauth"
      }
    },
